course: dictionary
lesson: 7948
title: Rebirth: a new start
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Break the word into its parts. «Re» means again, and «birth» is the start of life, so a rebirth is a new start, a return to life after something has ended. In spring, the cold winter is over and the trees and flowers come back to life. In science lessons, we call this a time of rebirth in nature.
explain: The context often tells you which meaning is meant. «The Renaissance, which means rebirth, began in Italy in the 1400s, when artists and thinkers grew excited again about the art and learning of ancient Greece and Rome.» Here rebirth means a revival: people became excited about old ideas again, so the old learning came back to life.
explain: Religions use the word too, but with care. «Priya says Hindus believe the soul is reborn in a new body» means that rebirth is what Hindus believe, not a fact everyone agrees on. Words like «believe» and «some people think» tell you that an idea is a belief.
explain: Notice the words around rebirth. «A rebirth of interest» means interest coming back to life, and «spiritual rebirth» means a new spiritual life. The context shows you which kind of new start the writer means.
fact: Rebirth means a new start, or a return to life after something has ended or declined.
fact: «Rebirth» can also mean a revival of an idea, art or place.
fact: Hindus and Buddhists believe in rebirth after death, which is called reincarnation.
fact: Christians speak of being «born again», a new spiritual life through faith.
fact: Words like «believe» and «some people think» show that an idea is a belief, not something proven for everyone.
exercise: «The Renaissance, which means rebirth, began in Italy in the 1400s.» What does rebirth mean here? | *A revival of art and learning | A broken old building | A cold winter with no spring | A kind of Italian pasta
exercise: «Priya says Hindus believe the soul is reborn in a new body.» What does reborn mean? | Lost in a dark forest | *Born again into a new life | Left behind for ever | Made of gold
exercise: Which word is the best swap for rebirth in «a rebirth of interest»? | Winter | Sadness | ending | *revival
test: «Christians speak of spiritual rebirth in baptism.» What does spiritual rebirth most likely mean? | A sudden loss of memory | *A new spiritual life through faith | A wet, grey day | Being very hungry
test: In «Mei's Buddhist grandma believes in rebirth», which word tells you this is a belief? | grandma | *believes | Buddhist | rebirth
exam: Why does the text say «many religions teach» rather than «it is true»? | Because everyone agrees on it | Because rebirth means cold weather | *Because these are beliefs, and no one can prove them for everyone | Because heaven is a made-up place
